{"subjectId":"c","id":"multi-dimensional-arrays","title":"Multi-dimensional Arrays","group":"Arrays & Strings","order":19,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">A 2-D array in C is an <em>array of arrays</em>, stored <strong>row by row</strong> (row-major) in one contiguous block.</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"c\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;\n\nint main(void) {\n    int m[2][3] = {\n        {1, 2, 3},\n        {4, 5, 6},\n    };\n    for (int r = 0; r &lt; 2; r++) {\n        for (int c = 0; c &lt; 3; c++) printf(\"%d \", m[r][c]);\n        printf(\"\\n\");\n    }\n    printf(\"sizeof m = %zu, sizeof m[0] = %zu\\n\", sizeof m, sizeof m[0]);\n\n    int *flat = &amp;m[0][0];               /* row-major: rows are laid end to end */\n    for (int i = 0; i &lt; 6; i++) printf(\"%d \", flat[i]);\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n    return 0;\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>1 2 3\n4 5 6\nsizeof m = 24, sizeof m[0] = 12\n1 2 3 4 5 6</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"formula\">address of <code>m[r][c]</code> = base + (r × COLS + c) × sizeof(element)</div>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrow-right\"></i>Passing a 2-D array to a function</h3>\n<p>All dimensions except the first must be known to the function, because the compiler needs the row length to compute <code>m[r][c]</code>.</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"c\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;\n\n#define COLS 3\n\nint trace_like_sum(int m[][COLS], int rows) {        /* fixed column count */\n    int s = 0;\n    for (int r = 0; r &lt; rows; r++)\n        for (int c = 0; c &lt; COLS; c++) s += m[r][c];\n    return s;\n}\n\nvoid print_matrix(int rows, int cols, int m[rows][cols]) {   /* C99 VLA parameter */\n    for (int r = 0; r &lt; rows; r++) {\n        for (int c = 0; c &lt; cols; c++) printf(\"%3d\", m[r][c]);\n        printf(\"\\n\");\n    }\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    int a[2][COLS] = {{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}};\n    printf(\"sum = %d\\n\", trace_like_sum(a, 2));\n    print_matrix(2, COLS, a);\n    return 0;\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>sum = 21\n  1  2  3\n  4  5  6</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-math-x-plus-x\"></i>Matrix multiplication</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"c\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;\n\nint main(void) {\n    int A[2][3] = {{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}};\n    int B[3][2] = {{7, 8}, {9, 10}, {11, 12}};\n    int C[2][2] = {{0}};\n    for (int i = 0; i &lt; 2; i++)\n        for (int j = 0; j &lt; 2; j++)\n            for (int k = 0; k &lt; 3; k++)\n                C[i][j] += A[i][k] * B[k][j];\n    printf(\"%d %d\\n%d %d\\n\", C[0][0], C[0][1], C[1][0], C[1][1]);\n    return 0;\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>58 64\n139 154</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list-letters\"></i>Arrays of strings</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"c\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;\n\nint main(void) {\n    char names[3][8] = {\"Ann\", \"Bob\", \"Charlie\"};    /* 2-D char array: 24 bytes */\n    const char *langs[] = {\"C\", \"Go\", \"Rust\"};       /* array of pointers */\n    for (int i = 0; i &lt; 3; i++) printf(\"%s/%s \", names[i], langs[i]);\n    printf(\"\\n%zu %zu\\n\", sizeof names, sizeof langs);\n    return 0;\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>Ann/C Bob/Go Charlie/Rust\n24 24</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th><code>char names[3][8]</code></th><th><code>const char *langs[3]</code></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3 × 8 bytes, each row a writable copy</td><td>3 pointers to string literals (read-only)</td></tr><tr><td>Rows have a fixed maximum length</td><td>Each string can have any length</td></tr><tr><td>Wastes space for short strings</td><td>Only pointer overhead</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Performance</div><p>Iterate row by row (<code>for r … for c …</code>) — row-major order visits memory sequentially and is cache-friendly. Swapping the loops on a big matrix can be several times slower.</p></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>How is int a[3][4] laid out in memory?</summary><div><p>As 12 consecutive <code>int</code>s: row 0 (4 ints), then row 1, then row 2. <code>a[i]</code> is an <code>int[4]</code> array, <code>a</code> decays to <code>int (*)[4]</code> (pointer to a row), and <code>a[i][j]</code> is <code>*(*(a + i) + j)</code>.</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Why must a function parameter for a 2-D array specify the column count?</summary><div><p>To compute the address of <code>m[r][c]</code> the compiler needs the length of each row (<code>r × COLS + c</code>). The first dimension is not needed because the parameter is really a pointer to a row.</p></div></details></section>"}